WEBVTT

00:04:57.528 --> 00:05:00.759
is by starting to ask
some fundamental questions

00:05:00.783 --> 00:05:02.787
about the status quo

00:05:02.811 --> 00:05:05.535
and whether we are happy
with the way it is.

00:05:06.529 --> 00:05:08.735
We need to begin asking
questions of ourselves

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:10.503
and of our elected officials,

00:05:10.527 --> 00:05:12.790
and I'd like to share
three with you today.

00:05:14.798 --> 00:05:16.996
The first one is,

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.099
"How much nuclear risk
are you willing to take or tolerate?"

00:05:22.805 --> 00:05:26.701
Right now, nuclear policy
depends on deterrence theory.

00:05:27.336 --> 00:05:29.058
Developed in the 1950s,

00:05:29.082 --> 00:05:31.750
the idea is that one
country's nuclear weapons